Description: Wayland VNC server and compatibility toolkit for RealVNC viewers
 wayland-vnc makes a native Wayland desktop reachable with actual RealVNC
 viewers. It installs a systemd user service that runs the WayVNC server inside
 the logged-in Wayland session, bound to this machine only (127.0.0.1:5900) until
 local network access is turned on in the settings app, plus provisioning helpers
 (`wayland-vnc set-password`, `provision`) and a read-only capability diagnostic
 (`wayland-vnc doctor`).
 .
 Installing enables and starts the service for every logged-in user; a random
 viewer password is generated on first start, so the server is never unauthenticated.
 View or change it in the Wayland VNC settings app, or with `wayland-vnc
 set-password`. To let a phone or another computer on the same Wi-Fi or LAN
 connect, turn on Local Network Access in the settings app: the server then binds
 every interface, and is reachable from every network this machine is on -- a user
 service cannot fence that, so do not forward the port from the internet.
 Per-desktop viewer qualification evidence lives upstream.
